      ],
      "hasPart": [
        {
          "@type": "HealthTopicContent",
          "description": "To avoid bad breath, it can help to brush your teeth and gums at least twice a day, clean your tongue once a day and use antibacterial mouthwash.",
          "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/SelfCareHealthAspect",
          "hasPart": [
            {
              "@type": "WebPageElement",
              "headline": "",
              "text": "<p>The best way of making sure you do not have bad breath is to keep your teeth, tongue and mouth clean.</p>"
            },
            {
              "@type": "WebPageElement",
              "headline": "Do",
              "text": "<ul><li><p>gently brush your teeth and gums at least twice a day for 2 minutes</p></li><li><p>use a fluoride toothpaste</p></li><li><p>gently clean your tongue once a day using a tongue scraper or cleaner</p></li><li><p>clean between your teeth with interdental brushes or floss at least once a day</p></li><li><p>get regular <a href=\"/live-well/healthy-teeth-and-gums/dental-check-ups/\">dental check-ups</a></p></li><li><p>keep <a href=\"/tests-and-treatments/dentures/\">dentures (false teeth)</a> clean and remove them at night</p></li><li><p>use sugar-free mints or chewing gum after having strong-smelling food and drinks</p></li><li><p>try using an antibacterial mouthwash or toothpaste</p></li></ul>"
            },
            {
              "@type": "WebPageElement",
              "headline": "Don't",
              "text": "<ul><li><p><a href=\"/live-well/quit-smoking/nhs-stop-smoking-services-help-you-quit/\">do not smoke</a></p></li><li><p>do not drink too much alcohol</p></li><li><p>do not rinse your mouth with water straight after brushing your teeth</p></li><li><p>do not have lots of sugary foods and drinks</p></li><li><p>do not brush so hard your gums or tongue bleed</p></li></ul>"
            }
          ],
          "headline": "How to treat bad breath yourself",
          "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/symptoms/bad-breath/#self-care"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HealthTopicContent",
          "description": "Causes of bad breath include eating strong-smelling or spicy foods, and problems with your teeth or gums, such as gum disease.",
          "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/CausesHealthAspect",
          "hasPart": [
            {
              "@type": "WebPageElement",
              "headline": "",
              "text": "<p>Causes of bad breath include:</p><ul><li>eating or drinking strong-smelling or spicy foods and drinks</li><li>problems with your teeth or gums, such as <a href=\"/conditions/gum-disease/\">gum disease</a>, holes in your teeth or an infection</li><li>fasting or crash dieting</li><li>some medical conditions, like <a href=\"/symptoms/dry-mouth/\">dry mouth</a>, <a href=\"/conditions/tonsillitis/\">tonsillitis</a> and <a href=\"/conditions/heartburn-and-acid-reflux/\">acid reflux</a></li><li>smoking</li></ul>"
            }
          ],
          "headline": "Causes of bad breath",
          "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/symptoms/bad-breath/#causes"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HealthTopicContent",
          "description": "",
          "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/MedicalHelpNonurgentHealthAspect",
          "hasPart": [
            {
              "@type": "WebPageElement",
              "headline": "See a dentist if you have:",
              "identifier": "primary",
              "text": "<ul>\n<li>\n  bad breath that does not go away after treating it yourself for a few weeks\n </li>\n<li>\n  painful, bleeding or swollen gums\n </li>\n<li>\n  toothache or wobbly adult teeth\n </li>\n<li>\n  problems with your dentures\n </li>\n</ul>\n"
            }
          ],
          "headline": "",
          "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/symptoms/bad-breath/#non-urgent-medical-help-old"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HealthTopicContent",
          "description": "Bad breath (sometimes called halitosis) is very common. You can usually treat it yourself by keeping your teeth, tongue and mouth clean.",
          "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/OverviewHealthAspect",
          "hasPart": [
            {
              "@type": "WebPageElement",
